BT /F2 16.00 Tf 52.00 220.70 Td (7. Conclusion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 196.70 Td (The three projects show different ways to design and run small terminal games. The first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 182.53 Td (Hangman project focuses on a straightforward implementation that is easy to follow. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 168.35 Td (second Hangman project expands the same game idea into a more formal object-oriented) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 154.18 Td (structure that demonstrates course learning outcomes such as abstraction, inheritance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 140.00 Td (polymorphism, and encapsulation. The Tic-Tac-Toe project applies object-oriented design) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 125.83 Td (to a board game simulation and adds richer terminal presentation and optional SSH-based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 111.65 Td (access.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 92.48 Td (Together, the projects demonstrate core programming techniques such as loops,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 52.00 78.30 Td (conditionals, state management, input validation, class design, dependency usage, and) Tj ET
